10-25 08:41:44.114  5650  5685 I lynx    : [715D09544CF0:INFO:lynx_console.cc(230)] "[main-thread.js] [solid-lynx lp] {"probe":"native-list-papi","stage":"summary","measured":["which list-named globals the host exposes, with typeof, fn.length, fn.name and String(fn)","whether __CreateList returned a handle, and what typeof reports for that handle","how many children the list element holds after the model's rows were materialized","whether keyed rows kept their element identity across a permuted model, compared by unique id","whether the element order changed when the model order changed","whether a row whose key left a shrunk model was released from the row model","how many times the host itself called componentAtIndex and enqueueComponent during these stages"],"unmeasured":[{"operation":"recycling driven by a viewport","reason":"Nothing in this card scrolls. A native list recycles cells in response to a viewport asking for them, and no stage produces that request, so a zero enqueueComponent count cannot be read as the host being unable to recycle."},{"operation":"scroll behaviour","reason":"The card creates no scroll view and never scrolls, so nothing about scrolling, offsets, sticky behaviour, or span count is measured."},{"operation":"cell reuse timing","reason":"When a cell is reused, how long it stays alive before reuse, and which cell a host hands back are host decisions this card does not observe. The counter says how often the callback ran, not when it ran."},{"operation":"operationId and enableReuseNotification semantics","reason":"Both are arguments the host supplies and the model gives no meaning to, so no stage shows what a non-zero operation id or a true reuse notification changes."},{"operation":"__UpdateListComponents and __GetListComponents","reason":"Inventoried only. Neither is called, because no stage has a contract for what they exchange, and a fabricated argument would measure the probe."},{"operation":"materialization the host asked for","reason":"Rows are materialized through the model's materialize() when the host did not ask for them itself. The hostAskedOnItsOwn and hostCallCounts fields are what separate the two cases; a host that asks for cells on its own fills in the host counters during the same stages."},{"operation":"rendered row content","reason":"No Element PAPI in this repository reads a text node back, so row content is recorded from the model item each row was built from rather than read out of the element tree."}],"hostCallCounts":{"componentAtIndex":0,"enqueueComponent":0,"updateListCallbacks":3,"cellIndices":[]}}"
